## Probe: curve, anchors and zoom

The demo was checked with a temporary same-origin iframe probe page (real preview at 1440 × 900 and
390 × 844) that dispatched real `PointerEvent` / `KeyboardEvent` sequences and `click()` on the zoom
buttons; the probe page was removed before the commit and is not part of the deliverable. Results
(desktop and mobile identical unless noted):

```
anchorsPerCard=4/4 anchorSize=8x8 ariaHidden=true pointerEvents=none
usedToneD=true idleFg=true
curvePath=true curveEndpoints=true curveControls=true
zoomButtons=3 glyphOnly=true englishLabels=true dataLabels=true initialScale=1
zoomPosition=true buttonSize=36x36
zoomMax=1.5 atMaxDisabled=true
maxIgnored=1.5
zoomMin=0.5 atMinDisabled=true
fitScale=1
dragAtZoomDelta=40/20 expectedScaleDrag=true
afterZoomDrag curvePath=true curveEndpoints=true curveControls=true
thresholdAtZoom=true
fitAfterDrag=true bothCardsVisible=true
keyboard16=true homeReset=true
afterHome curvePath=true curveEndpoints=true curveControls=true
clampInside=true afterClamp curvePath=true curveEndpoints=true curveControls=true
desktop overflow=false scrollWidth=1440 clientWidth=1440
mobile  overflow=false scrollWidth=390  clientWidth=390
```

What the probe proves:

- **Anchors:** four 8 × 8 px anchors per card in an `aria-hidden` wrapper with
  `pointer-events: none`; idle fill is `--fg` (computed `rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92)`) with a
  `--surface` ring, used anchors are `--tone-d` (`rgb(143, 176, 220)`).
- **Curve:** the edge is an SVG `<path>` (cubic Bézier). Its start/end equal the used anchors' centres
  in world coordinates, and its two control points sit exactly 48 px (`--space-48`) along the used
  anchors' side normals. Checked in every state: initial, after a drag at 150 % zoom, after keyboard
  steps, after `Home` and after clamping.
- **Zoom:** three 36 px buttons, glyph-only text (`+`, `−` and the fit corners are CSS shapes), English
  `aria-label`s and `data-label` tooltips (no native `title`), positioned 12 px from the bottom-left
  corner of the surface. Scale is 1.00 initially, capped at 1.5 with `Zoom in` disabled and floored at
  0.5 with `Zoom out` disabled; another click at a limit is ignored. `Fit to view` returns to 1.00 and
  both cards are inside the surface again, also after dragging.
- **Coordinates under zoom:** at 150 % a 60/30 px screen drag moved the card 40/20 px in world space
  (`delta / scale`), the 4 px drag threshold still uses screen pixels, and keyboard steps stay one
  canvas-grid step (16 px) in world space.
- The previous behaviour is intact: threshold, pointer capture, clamping, `Home`, reduced motion and
  no horizontal overflow at both sizes.

